\description{
Builds a manuscript-ready, multi-panel figure illustrating the internal
steps of the legacy workflow (\code{\link[=define.flow.control]{define.flow.control()}}, \code{\link[=clean.controls]{clean.controls()}},
\code{\link[=get.fluorophore.spectra]{get.fluorophore.spectra()}}) for one or more single-stained control
samples: the automated scatter gate, autofluorescence-exclusion gating,
scatter-matched universal-negative selection, and the robust linear model
fit used to extract the fluorophore's spectral signature. Uses the same
building blocks as the rest of AutoSpectral (\code{\link[=create.biplot]{create.biplot()}}-style
biexponential biplots, \code{\link[=scatter.match.plot]{scatter.match.plot()}}) so panel styling matches
the package's other figures.

This function runs the full legacy pipeline itself -- it calls
\code{\link[=define.flow.control]{define.flow.control()}} and \code{\link[=clean.controls]{clean.controls()}} internally for the entire
control set in \code{control.def.file}, not just the illustrated
fluorophore(s) -- so it can be slow for large panels. \code{parallel = FALSE}
is used internally throughout, since diagnostic capture is unreliable
under forked parallel processing.

Requires \code{plot_spectra_automated_steps.R} and
\code{plot_spectra_standard_workflow.R} to be loaded in the same package
namespace (several private helpers are shared), and requires the
\code{diagnostics.env}-aware versions of \code{remove.af()} / \code{run.af.removal()} /
\code{clean.controls()}.
}
